    <string name="scene_info_lcdon_title">lcdon</string>
    <string name="scene_info_lcdon_body">Inferred from naming and common power-management semantics: parameters under lcdon may apply when the screen is on. Actual behavior depends on the system implementation.</string>
    <string name="scene_info_lcdoff_title">lcdoff</string>
    <string name="scene_info_lcdoff_body">Inferred from naming and common power-management semantics: parameters under lcdoff may apply when the screen is off. Actual behavior depends on the system implementation.</string>
    <string name="scene_info_night_title">night</string>
    <string name="scene_info_night_body">Inferred from naming and common power-management semantics: parameters under night may apply during night/sleep schedules. Actual behavior depends on the system implementation.</string>
    <string name="scene_info_charging_title">charging</string>
    <string name="scene_info_charging_body">Inferred from naming and common power-management semantics: parameters under charging may apply while charging. Vendor behavior may be more aggressive or conservative. Actual behavior depends on the system implementation.</string>
    <string name="scene_info_extremefg_title">extremeFg</string>
    <string name="scene_info_extremefg_body">Inferred from naming and common power-management semantics: extremeFg may represent a foreground-intensive grouping. It may enforce stricter or looser handling for active apps. Actual behavior depends on the system implementation.</string>
    <string name="scene_info_fastfreeze_title">fastFreeze</string>
    <string name="scene_info_fastfreeze_body">Inferred from naming and common power-management semantics: fastFreeze may shorten delay and enter freezing faster. Actual behavior depends on the system implementation.</string>
    <string name="scene_info_minsystem_title">minSystem</string>
    <string name="scene_info_minsystem_body">Inferred from naming and common power-management semantics: minSystem may represent a lower bound for protecting critical system components from freezing. Actual behavior depends on the system implementation.</string>
